530, 1553, 1639, 1776]}, "result_digest": "3c6aad8254ae6b98", "result_summary": "{\"counts\": [{\"n_events\": 195, \"window\": [8963, 13962]}, {\"n_events\": 98, \"window\": [13963, 18962]}]}", "latency_ms": 3, "tokens_before": 61434, "tokens_after": 61434, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_8b4a3bfa", "decision": "present", "mechanism": "regime_switch", "entities": [323, 477, 865, 889, 1039, 1119, 1389, 1432, 1530, 1553, 1639, 1776], "window": [246, 30246], "confidence": 0.75, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "Neighborhood-evolution analysis (half-window 5000) finds a marked peak change (peak_change = 0.3023) at time 13963, indicating an abrupt replacement of roughly 30% of the group's contacts around that time (step_01). Event counts and graph summaries for the two half-windows ([8963,13962] vs [13963,18962]) show a drop in activity and fewer distinct edges after the candidate change (steps_16, 02, 03), which could confound naive interpretations but do not explain away the concentrated change detected. Static neighbor lists over the full interval (example: node 323, step_04) show many persistent ties when time is ignored, so the observed shift is temporal (a regime switch) rather than merely an artifact of static connectivity. Overall the temporal evidence supports an abrupt regime change in the group's contacts."}, "raw_final_response": "{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_8b4a3bfa\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [323, 477, 865, 889, 1039, 1119, 1389, 1432, 1530, 1553, 1639, 1776],\n  \"window\": [246, 30246],\n  \"confidence\": 0.75,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Neighborhood-evolution analysis (half-window 5000) finds a marked peak change (peak_change = 0.3023) at time 13963, indicating an abrupt replacement of roughly 30% of the group's contacts around that time (step_01). Event counts and graph summaries for the two half-windows ([8963,13962] vs [13963,18962]) show a drop in activity and fewer distinct edges after the candidate change (steps_16, 02, 03), which could confound naive interpretations but do not explain away the concentrated change detected. Static neighbor lists over the full interval (example: node 323, step_04) show many persistent ties when time is ignored, so the observed shift is temporal (a regime switch) rather than merely an artifact of static connectivity. Overall the temporal evidence supports an abrupt regime change in the group's contacts.\"\n}", "total_input_tokens": 66836, "total_output_tokens": 7911, "total_tokens": 74747, "total_latency_ms": 120389, "llm_calls": 17, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}